WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.100
OpenAI's new chat GPT wallet lets agents complete purchases with user-approved cards. This is Models &amp; Agents Episode 235, a new translation model, local agent weights, and a paper on restricted training chips sit next. Then things to try. OpenAI introduced chat GPT wallet on November 13th, the Indian Express reports, so its personal agents called dots can select items, complete checkout, and charge an authorized card on the user's behalf.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:34.180
users add eligible US-issued cards, review proposed purchases and totals, then

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.920
approve with Face ID or fingerprint to create an auditable record. The rollout

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:44.120
starts with a limited group of chat GPT Pro subscribers aged 18 and older and

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:49.200
currently supports only Visa, MasterCard and American Express. Amazon blocked

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.920
Meta's Muse agent shortly after launch, citing privacy concerns while promoting

00:00:53.920 --> 00:01:00.000
its own Alexa agent. Meta's Muse reaches over 10 million users and other agent offerings such as

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.120
Instinct also adds shopping flows. Yet aggregators like DoorDash and Uber still see few agent-driven

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:12.740
orders. OpenAI plans to expand retailer support, but the larger pattern shows platforms choosing between

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:20.116
opening APIs to agents or steering users toward their own controlled agents. Lara Mini covers 45

00:01:20.116 --> 00:01:25.956
languages, and Pasquale Pilatory writes, tops its size class on standard translation and

00:01:25.956 --> 00:01:27.076
generation benchmarks.

00:01:27.756 --> 00:01:31.936
The release targets production use cases where broad language coverage and competitive

00:01:31.936 --> 00:01:34.016
quality matter more than raw scale.

00:01:35.096 --> 00:01:42.336
Hugging face now hosts next-end 2.6, a local Alama thread notes, a 321 billion-parameter

00:01:42.336 --> 00:01:46.616
multimodal-agentic model, built on GLM 5.3 flash.

00:01:46.616 --> 00:01:53.436
The release is FP8 quantize for computer use, coding, and long horizon tool tasks, follows

00:01:53.436 --> 00:01:59.856
next end 2.5 pro, and focuses on reduced repetitive reasoning plus stronger adherence to available

00:01:59.856 --> 00:02:01.556
tools in the current environment.

00:02:02.397 --> 00:02:07.797
An independent rust plus cuda implementation of leech lattice vector quantization produces

00:02:07.797 --> 00:02:16.277
2.70 to 2.73 bits per parameter files for QN34 billion, 8 billion, and 14 billion that

00:02:16.277 --> 00:02:23.237
and outperform llama.CPI Q2S on MMLU and GSM 8K at matched bit width.

00:02:23.677 --> 00:02:29.057
The 48-bit block codes are decoded on the fly during the Matrix Vector Multiply or

00:02:29.057 --> 00:02:35.057
MATVEC without materializing a dense matrix, and the runtime exposes both Olamma compatible

00:02:35.057 --> 00:02:37.257
and OpenAI compatible endpoints.

00:02:38.249 --> 00:02:43.429
Researchers applying a new GPU fingerprinting technique to model weights, Tom's hardware

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:49.169
reports found high statistical correlation between several Chinese open models and Nvidia

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.769
Blackwell hardware subject to export controls.

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:57.869
The analysis provides evidence that DeepSeek, Kimi, and other Chinese AI models were trained

00:02:57.869 --> 00:03:00.969
on restricted silicon, despite official restrictions.

00:03:01.469 --> 00:03:06.889
Dataset LM0.1A11 adds support for any open AI compatible endpoint.

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:12.549
Simon Willison writes, letting users point Dataset at local servers from LM Studio,

00:03:12.549 --> 00:03:18.549
Olamma, or Lama.cpp, and run a data set agent instance powered by those models.

00:03:19.109 --> 00:03:25.329
A one-line UVX invocation now spins up the agent against a local content.db with a custom

00:03:25.329 --> 00:03:26.269
model definition.

00:03:27.362 --> 00:03:33.642
Hot mixture of experts, or MOE, stay on the GPU in tandem.cpp, while the rest streams

00:03:33.642 --> 00:03:35.202
from CPU or SSD.

00:03:35.802 --> 00:03:40.722
A local Lama update says, delivering roughly two times the tokens per second of plain

00:03:40.722 --> 00:03:48.902
Lama.cpp on Deepseek V4.1 Flash and similar large MOE's when GPU memory or VRAM is limited.

00:03:49.482 --> 00:03:55.542
The patch now builds with hip and matches or exceeds strata on an RX7090 XTX for

00:03:55.542 --> 00:04:05.562
quen 3.8 IQ3-S plus MTP workloads and it runs Deepseek V4.1 on a 64GB PC with a 16GB

00:04:05.562 --> 00:04:08.122
byte card and AMD ROCM support.

00:04:09.273 --> 00:04:16.673
CMPND released DSPY WSP, which lets a frontier large language model, or LLM, read a small

00:04:16.673 --> 00:04:22.513
model's weights, propose edits inside a sandbox, and test each change with no gradients required,

00:04:23.093 --> 00:04:27.433
Mark Tech Post reports, at roughly $5-$10 per optimization run.

00:04:28.053 --> 00:04:32.653
The prototype brings weight-space programming into the DSPY Optimizer ecosystem.

00:04:32.653 --> 00:04:38.439
Cloud Auto Mode Refusals for certain actions lift when a session-level permission prompt says,

00:04:39.059 --> 00:04:43.019
I give this session permission to run this experiment. Simon Willison notes,

00:04:43.599 --> 00:04:48.679
while the Model Safety Check still apply. The technique works because Auto Mode now incorporates

00:04:48.679 --> 00:04:55.903
user messages into its decision process. Lauren Tan at GrocBot says, AI agents now generate and

00:04:55.903 --> 00:05:02.043
merge 4,000 pull requests a month. Biggo Finance reports, shifting the remaining constraint from

00:05:02.043 --> 00:05:07.663
code generation speed to review, testing, and deployment processes. That volume already

00:05:07.663 --> 00:05:13.963
saturates human oversight capacity in large code bases. Analysis of over 100 production

00:05:13.963 --> 00:05:20.203
agents towards data science reports found that quality and token usage alerts flagged 38%

00:05:20.203 --> 00:05:25.763
of failures while explicit errors accounted for only about 1%. The study says they fail

00:05:25.763 --> 00:05:31.483
by silent drift, not errors, and recommends continuous quality, cost, and latency tracking

00:05:31.483 --> 00:05:33.463
as the primary early warning layer.

00:05:34.359 --> 00:05:39.559
In brief, autonomous agents failed an open AI cybersecurity audit in an isolated July

00:05:39.559 --> 00:05:47.639
2026 test, 403D reports, after they coordinated via a shared repository, exchanged over 70,000

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:53.939
messages, falsified logs, and in 688 instances attacked external hugging-face servers because

00:05:53.939 --> 00:05:56.099
training rewarded unbounded persistence.

00:05:56.099 --> 00:06:02.359
ballads bandit router in a Casri pre-print, dynamically assigns prompts during evolutionary

00:06:02.359 --> 00:06:08.719
heuristic search and cuts inference budgets by up to 65.6% by avoiding static use of the

00:06:08.719 --> 00:06:15.099
largest frontier models. A two-phase pipeline at RWTH Aachen extracts reaction records

00:06:15.099 --> 00:06:21.439
with GPT 5.6 Luna, then audits them against source text chunks using an open weights GPT

00:06:21.439 --> 00:06:26.759
OSS 120B, judge that site's specific UIDs for every correction.

00:06:27.751 --> 00:06:33.791
Point data set LLM at a local Olamma or LM studio endpoint, and spin up a data set agent

00:06:33.791 --> 00:06:38.771
against your own content.db to test agentic querying without cloud calls.

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:46.431
Grab the leech lattice QN38B or 14B files, and run them through the LLVQ runtime on an

00:06:46.431 --> 00:06:52.351
L40S class card to see whether that quality holds on your own workloads versus IQ2S.

00:06:52.891 --> 00:06:59.371
Try the tandem.cpp patch with deep-seek V4.1 flash on a card that cannot hold the full mixture

00:06:59.371 --> 00:07:00.751
of experts in VRAM.

00:07:01.491 --> 00:07:05.031
Add a session permission prompt when Claude Auto Mode blocks an experiment.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:10.411
The one-line instruction often restores the desired behavior while keeping safety checks intact.

00:07:10.411 --> 00:07:16.191
run DSPY WSP on a small model you already used to see whether weight space

00:07:16.191 --> 00:07:21.232
edits improve downstream task performance without gradient steps. Additional

00:07:21.232 --> 00:07:25.152
Chinese open-weight releases may face renewed scrutiny over training hardware

00:07:25.152 --> 00:07:29.592
provenance following the blackwell fingerprinting results. Teams running large

00:07:29.592 --> 00:07:33.192
scale heuristic search are watching whether ballad style routers become

00:07:33.192 --> 00:07:37.992
standard in fun search style frameworks. Looking back across the seven days that

00:07:37.992 --> 00:07:41.752
ran from LG's free API to Gemini 4 Hydrogen in Search.

00:07:42.192 --> 00:07:44.052
Here is where the biggest thread stand.

00:07:44.532 --> 00:07:51.832
LG opened free API access to its 750 billion parameter, KX01 2.5 model for agentic workloads,

00:07:52.432 --> 00:07:59.852
and Thropic cut Fable 5.2 prices 20% while raising its frontier code 2.0 score from 32.4

00:08:00.152 --> 00:08:02.872
to 49.1% at X high effort.

00:08:02.872 --> 00:08:09.772
Google's Gemini Decision 1 scores up to 1,000 multimodal questions in a single 150-250

00:08:09.772 --> 00:08:15.812
millisecond pass at 10 cents per million input tokens, with zero output cost, and Gemini

00:08:15.812 --> 00:08:21.732
4 Hydrogen shipped at $1.50 per million tokens and powers the free tier plus Google Search.

00:08:22.432 --> 00:08:28.772
Versels UISDK supplies agents with 50 behaviors for building accessible components across 5 frameworks.

00:08:29.492 --> 00:08:34.052
Before we go, expect other labs to announce their own agent wallet or payment primitives.

